137:- `contract-cli-surface` — direct: The Sprint 33 implementation conforms to the CLI Surface contract across all nine requirement IDs. CLI-SHAPE-001 is met: the code-context stage is a value integrated uniformly into `prompt`, `validate`, `flow`, `status`, and stable JSON projections rather than a parallel command family (`target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:78-181`, `target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:182-230`). CLI-HELP-001 is met: `--help` is honored at the root and per-subcommand level with stage-specific help text listing `code-context` alongside the other planning stages (`target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:30-62`, `target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:1052-1106`, `target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:1139-1156`). CLI-IO-001 is met: result data goes to stdout (prompt preview, status, flow output, validate, JSON envelopes) while progress, lifecycle events, and smoke progress go to stderr (`target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:312-317`, `target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:350-361`, `target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:426-449`). CLI-EXIT-001 is met: stable classified exit codes (ExitOK, ExitUsage, ExitValidation, ExitRuntime, ExitWorkspace, ExitConfig, ExitCancel, ExitPartial) are used consistently across commands (`target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:146`, `:212`, `:269`, `:296`, `:331`, `:381`). CLI-JSON-001 is met: every JSON-emitting command uses the same `{schema_version:1, operation, status, result, [error]}` envelope and rejects trailing output (`target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:97`, `:103`, `:203`, `:210`, `:227`, `:257`, `:325`, `:373`; test `target/internal/app/sprint_commands_test.go:106-133`). CLI-CONFIG-001 is met: precedence defaults < workspace < env < CLI is enforced, redaction is applied to known secret markers and to display paths, and effective values are surfaced in both text and JSON modes with the source map preserved (`target/internal/platform/config/config.go:107-156`, `target/internal/platform/config/redaction.go:23-43`, `target/internal/app/config_commands.go:42-87`). CLI-LIFE-001 is met: caller-owned `context.Context` is propagated through service, runner, and web operation seams; cancellation, timeout, and cleanup-uncertain outcomes are mapped to distinct terminal states (`target/internal/sprint/code_context.go:270-275`, `target/internal/sprint/code_context.go:316-330`, `target/internal/sprint/code_context.go:346-395`, `target/internal/app/operations.go:265-390`). CLI-SAFE-001 is met: `--dry-run` is accepted on `flow --to code-context`, atomic candidate promotion preserves the last valid artifact on failed rerun, and `--force-review` requires an explicit `--override-reason` rationale (`target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:182-230`, `target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:489-512`, `target/internal/sprint/code_context.go:237-307`). CLI-NONINT-001 is met: smoke requires `--yes`/`--non-interactive`, code-context flow does not block on prompts, and prompt/validate/status are deterministic offline reads (`target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:190-192`, `:347-348`; tests `target/internal/sprint/code_context_test.go:180-223`, `target/internal/app/sprint_commands_test.go:176-350`).
138:- `contract-configuration` — direct: Sprint 33 correctly applies the Configuration contract to the new code-context stage settings. The Planning struct in `target/internal/platform/config/config.go` adds `CodeContextModel` and `CodeContextVariant` typed fields with `json:"code_context_model"`/`json:"code_context_variant"` tags (lines 41-42), explicit source initialization to "default" (line 135), workspace YAML parsing precedence (lines 297-300 in `setField`), and prefixed environment variable overrides `ULTRAPLAN_CODE_CONTEXT_MODEL`/`ULTRAPLAN_CODE_CONTEXT_VARIANT` (lines 117-118). `Validate()` (line 377) is invoked at the end of `Load()` before any consumer sees the config (line 152), satisfying CFG-START-001. Redaction applies the existing safe-projection rules to the new fields via `RedactValue` in `target/internal/platform/config/redaction.go:51-52`. The `config show` CLI projection in `target/internal/app/config_commands.go:57-58` reports the effective values together with their source labels, supporting CFG-OBS-001. The runtime wiring in `target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:531-551` applies the documented stage-specific fallback (`Planning.CodeContextModel` -> `Models.Primary` -> `Models.Default`; `Planning.CodeContextVariant` -> `Execution.DefaultVariant`) and passes the result to the existing `StageRuntime` map. Tests in `target/internal/platform/config/config_test.go` cover workspace/env/CLI precedence, env-over-workspace precedence for code-context, source tracking at `Sources["planning.code_context_model"]`, and code-context redaction (lines 33-34, 47-49, 72, 81, 89-90). The implementation inherits the existing pre-sprint pattern of substring-heuristic secret detection rather than explicit field marking; this is the project's pre-existing redaction rule and is applied consistently to the new code-context fields as called out in `requirements.md` row 'Configuration redaction'.
140:- `contract-errors` — direct: The errors contract is partially conformant. The implementation distinguishes lifecycle states (StageStatus, LatestOutcome, ExecuteTaskStatus, AttemptStatus, OperationState) and uses sentinel errors for malformed/unsupported flow state, atomic write with restore on persistence failure (target/internal/sprint/code_context.go:346-395), explicit runtime-required failures before runtime invocation (target/internal/sprint/code_context.go:234-236, target/internal/sprint/service.go:476-481), and a bounded corrective retry path for LLM output validation (target/internal/sprint/service.go:1002-1016). However, the implementation does not produce a structured OperationalError with the required canonical fields (code, category, severity, retryable, details, correlation_id, trace_id, cause, causes, timestamp). Error codes are derived from err.Error() substring matching in failedOperation (target/internal/app/operations.go:615-625) and mapSprintError (target/internal/app/sprint_commands.go:595-601), the translated Cause field duplicates Message, the StageState.Error field is a plain string with no code/component/operation, safeError truncates to 180 chars without redaction, raw error strings are forwarded to user-facing progress callbacks, and the HTTP error envelope drops cause and category. Re-review is required after the structured-error migration.
